      "stageRecord": "In the ordinary Turkish reading, the sentence means ‘Ali read the book.’ The verb selects an internal Theme argument, kitabı, whose final vowel marks accusative case. The nominal is represented as an NP, following an NP-based version of X-bar Theory; its inflected word is retained intact rather than decomposed into morphological terminals. Turkish head-final order places this object before V within V′. The proper name Ali forms a separate NP, available as the external argument. The verb is initially represented by the stem oku, before its combination with finite inflection. Although kitabı can have a possessive interpretation in other environments, that interpretation is not an alternative object analysis here: a third-person possessive definite object would require kitabını.",
