      "stageRecord": "The VP combines with a following finite I head carrying past tense and third-person singular agreement, yielding head-final I′. Ali is introduced in Spec-IP. This analysis adopts the traditional GB placement of the external argument directly in Spec-IP, rather than a VP-internal subject hypothesis, so it does not posit subject movement or a subject trace. The verbal predicate assigns Ali its external Agent role, and finite I licenses nominative case on the subject. The object retains its Theme role and accusative licensing. The abstract inflection has not yet received its overt exponent; this workspace explicitly provides both the verb's source position and the higher inflectional head required for the next operation.",
