      "stageRecord": "The verb raises from the previously established V position to the immediately higher I head, leaving a silent head trace. Head adjunction places the verb before inflection, preserving Turkish stem–suffix order. This is a V-to-I analysis of the finite form, not an analysis with lowering of I onto an unmoved verb; the surface string alone does not decide between those theoretical implementations. Following head movement, past inflection receives the suffixal exponent -du, selected by Turkish vowel harmony and the phonological environment of oku. Third-person singular has no additional overt agreement suffix here. The stem and inflection jointly realize the single input word okudu. The verbal chain preserves the object's theta and Case relations, and its trace is locally antecedent-governed by the raised head without an intervening head. Ali remains the nominative Agent in Spec-IP. The completed IP is grammatical: both overt NPs are Case-licensed, each argument has one theta role, and no scrambling, A-movement of an NP, or binding dependency is required. The pronounced order is subject, accusative object, finite verb.",
